        "text": "每日一诗103\n\nSomething is too short as life.\nIt's not I refuse to tell it clearly,\nIt's I don't get some privilege.\nWhen the first sunrise came to me,\nI thought it would never vanish.\nYet even the dearest perish,\nAnd the only pleasure may be,\nSadness won't remain forever too."
